1
00:00:01,100 --> 00:00:01,667
<i>What are you doing?
Why do you look like that?</i>

2
00:00:01,800 --> 00:00:02,933
<i>[THUDS]
Let's go.</i>

3
00:00:03,067 --> 00:00:04,900
<i>Who gave you the right
to interfere with my affairs?</i>

4
00:00:05,033 --> 00:00:07,367
<i>We are just businessmen
closing a deal,</i>

5
00:00:07,500 --> 00:00:09,400
<i>so now, let's begin
the transaction.</i>

6
00:00:09,533 --> 00:00:11,600
<i>Wait, you'll face two big
syndicates.</i>

7
00:00:11,733 --> 00:00:12,700
<i>Only four of you
are storming in?</i>

8
00:00:12,833 --> 00:00:15,633
<i>This handoff is quick,
but we still planned it.</i>

9
00:00:15,767 --> 00:00:16,500
<i>[MULTIPLE GUNFIRE]
What was that?</i>

10
00:00:16,633 --> 00:00:18,433
<i> DDE! Open the door!</i>

11
00:00:18,567 --> 00:00:20,867
<i> Damn you, Zoey! I trusted you!</i>

12
00:00:21,000 --> 00:00:23,967
<i>You still have time to change,
Francis, surrender now!</i>

13
00:00:24,100 --> 00:00:25,433
<i>You're the ones who should
surrender!</i>

14
00:00:25,567 --> 00:00:26,867
<i> You entered the wrong den!</i>

15
00:00:27,000 --> 00:00:28,133
<i> They shouldn't get away.</i>

16
00:00:28,267 --> 00:00:30,633
<i>I didn't know you were
that good at fighting, Joey.</i>

17
00:00:30,767 --> 00:00:33,833
<i>My father taught me.
Thank you for saving me.</i>

18
00:00:34,000 --> 00:00:35,200
<i> I'm just doing my job.</i>

19
00:00:35,333 --> 00:00:37,300
<i>Francis Toledo,
you are under arrest.</i>

20
00:00:37,433 --> 00:00:39,300
<i>The DDE raided the transaction
in Valmora.</i>

21
00:00:39,433 --> 00:00:41,533
<i>The items and money were seized.
Everything was lost.</i>

22
00:00:41,667 --> 00:00:42,833
<i> Boss is wounded.</i>

23
00:00:44,033 --> 00:00:44,867
<i> Why, Boss?</i>

24
00:00:45,000 --> 00:00:46,433
<i>One of my cufflinks is missing.</i>

25
00:00:46,567 --> 00:00:50,500
<i>A person too private is often
hiding many things.</i>

26
00:00:50,633 --> 00:00:52,900
<i> Why don't you like Sir Tomas?</i>

27
00:00:53,033 --> 00:00:57,033
<i>Just remember,
do not trust Tomas.</i>

28
00:00:57,167 --> 00:00:58,500
<i> Do you have news?</i>

29
00:00:58,633 --> 00:01:02,800
<i>I'm sick of their excuses
about your father's corpse.</i>

30
00:01:02,933 --> 00:01:05,300
<i>I wanted to tell you something.</i>

31
00:01:05,433 --> 00:01:07,233
<i>What's the problem?
[GATE CREAKS]</i>

32
00:01:07,400 --> 00:01:08,400
<i> What is that?</i>

33
00:01:30,500 --> 00:01:31,400
[STIRRING MUSIC PLAYING]

34
00:01:31,533 --> 00:01:34,667
<i>Some truths are dangerous
to deliver.</i>

35
00:01:34,800 --> 00:01:36,000
<i> [CROWD CLAMORING]</i>

36
00:01:36,133 --> 00:01:38,600
<i> You've made enemies,</i>

37
00:01:38,733 --> 00:01:41,200
<i>and if something were
to happen to you,</i>

38
00:01:41,367 --> 00:01:44,267
<i> they wouldn't be surprised.</i>

39
00:01:44,400 --> 00:01:45,433
<i> Mom?</i>

40
00:01:47,000 --> 00:01:48,100
Andrew...

41
00:01:48,233 --> 00:01:51,933
What are you doing here?
You might get cold.

42
00:01:52,067 --> 00:01:55,267
I'm just getting some air.
What brought you here?

43
00:01:56,933 --> 00:01:59,900
I brought your favorite cake.

44
00:02:00,267 --> 00:02:02,133
I'm sure you miss this.

45
00:02:02,267 --> 00:02:07,533
That's what I used to send
to your office.

46
00:02:07,667 --> 00:02:08,533
[SENTIMENTAL MUSIC PLAYING]

47
00:02:08,667 --> 00:02:10,733
Of course, I remember.

48
00:02:13,167 --> 00:02:14,533
Thank you, son.

49
00:02:20,433 --> 00:02:21,467
You're welcome, Mom.

50
00:02:22,167 --> 00:02:23,133
You know,

51
00:02:23,667 --> 00:02:28,133
before, you always told me
that when you got a job,

52
00:02:28,267 --> 00:02:30,100
you'd always bring me this.

53
00:02:30,233 --> 00:02:31,767
And I told you...

54
00:02:32,800 --> 00:02:38,733
"How? You're stubborn.
You won't get a job."

55
00:02:42,767 --> 00:02:44,167
Look at me now, Mom.

56
00:02:45,233 --> 00:02:46,767
I have a career.

57
00:02:47,900 --> 00:02:50,467
And did you know...

58
00:02:50,600 --> 00:02:53,333
I followed your footsteps
because...

59
00:02:53,467 --> 00:02:55,433
I wanted you to be proud of me?

60
00:02:55,567 --> 00:02:56,867
I promise you, Mom,

61
00:02:57,000 --> 00:03:00,233
I won't use my profession
for selfishness.

62
00:03:02,033 --> 00:03:04,833
And of course,
I carry your name.

63
00:03:04,967 --> 00:03:07,333
So, I will never taint it.

64
00:03:09,600 --> 00:03:12,033
Mom, did you know...

65
00:03:12,167 --> 00:03:16,533
the case I'm handling now
is the biggest drug syndicate

66
00:03:16,667 --> 00:03:19,933
here in the Philippines,
Berdugo?

67
00:03:21,500 --> 00:03:25,233
[UNEASY MUSIC PLAYING]

68
00:03:25,367 --> 00:03:26,967
And, Mom, I'm close.

69
00:03:27,100 --> 00:03:28,733
I'll meet him,

70
00:03:29,900 --> 00:03:33,433
and I'll use everything
I learned from you

71
00:03:33,567 --> 00:03:39,500
to expose him and make him pay
for all his crimes.

72
00:03:44,300 --> 00:03:45,433
My child...

73
00:03:46,467 --> 00:03:48,233
Wait...

74
00:03:48,367 --> 00:03:49,633
What will you do?

75
00:03:49,767 --> 00:03:53,000
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

76
00:03:53,133 --> 00:03:56,833
Child, wait. Hey, dear, wait.
Call the police.

77
00:03:57,000 --> 00:04:02,467
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC CONTINUES]

78
00:04:04,333 --> 00:04:07,433
[DOOR RATTLING]

79
00:04:10,000 --> 00:04:10,867
Joey!

80
00:04:11,000 --> 00:04:11,867
Dad...

81
00:04:13,967 --> 00:04:17,867
[EMOTIONAL MUSIC PLAYING]

82
00:04:18,000 --> 00:04:19,000
Miguel?

83
00:04:23,633 --> 00:04:25,333
Miguel...

84
00:04:25,467 --> 00:04:26,500
Miguel...

85
00:04:26,633 --> 00:04:36,600
[EMOTIONAL MUSIC CONTINUES]

86
00:04:39,133 --> 00:04:40,933
Mom...

87
00:04:41,400 --> 00:04:42,700
Are you okay?

88
00:04:44,600 --> 00:04:45,900
Yeah,

89
00:04:46,033 --> 00:04:46,900
I'm okay.

90
00:04:48,133 --> 00:04:49,967
I'm just happy about...

91
00:04:51,833 --> 00:04:53,767
what you're doing.

92
00:04:55,800 --> 00:04:59,433
Because I never thought...

93
00:04:59,567 --> 00:05:02,867
that you'd turn your life around
like this.

94
00:05:04,567 --> 00:05:06,467
Son, you might overdo it.

95
00:05:06,600 --> 00:05:08,233
No, Mom.

96
00:05:09,733 --> 00:05:11,033
You know what, Mom?

97
00:05:11,167 --> 00:05:15,067
Let's go inside,
you might catch the dew here.

98
00:05:15,200 --> 00:05:16,533
Okay.

99
00:05:16,667 --> 00:05:17,700
Let's go?

100
00:05:17,833 --> 00:05:19,233
All right.

101
00:05:19,367 --> 00:05:20,733
Let's go, Mom.

102
00:05:21,833 --> 00:05:28,267
[PENSIVE MUSIC CONTINUES]

103
00:05:30,767 --> 00:05:31,867
Miguel.

104
00:05:32,000 --> 00:05:33,233
Wait.

105
00:05:36,433 --> 00:05:37,467
You're alive?

106
00:05:39,900 --> 00:05:42,767
Joey, your father is here.

107
00:05:48,533 --> 00:05:51,367
Mom, I'm sorry,
I've known for a long time.

108
00:05:51,500 --> 00:05:53,433
[SENTIMENTAL MUSIC PLAYING]

109
00:05:53,567 --> 00:05:57,133
I was going to tell you.
I was going to tell you earlier.

110
00:05:58,833 --> 00:06:01,733
Sorry for keeping it secret.

111
00:06:01,867 --> 00:06:03,467
It's okay, dear.

112
00:06:03,600 --> 00:06:05,867
I understand.

113
00:06:06,000 --> 00:06:08,300
Just don't do it again.

114
00:06:13,900 --> 00:06:15,033
How can I?

115
00:06:15,167 --> 00:06:19,700
When there's no room for anger
in my heart now.

116
00:06:19,833 --> 00:06:21,833
I'm just happy you're here,
Miguel.

117
00:06:21,967 --> 00:06:24,000
You're alive.

118
00:06:24,133 --> 00:06:26,867
Thank you so much
for understanding, Clarissa.

119
00:06:27,000 --> 00:06:28,133
I don't understand.

120
00:06:28,267 --> 00:06:31,100
Why did you have to pretend you
were dead?

121
00:06:31,233 --> 00:06:34,833
Because if I'm dead,
no one will look for me.

122
00:06:35,867 --> 00:06:39,067
I can move more freely
to find Berdugo,

123
00:06:40,100 --> 00:06:42,300
and you won't be in danger.

124
00:06:47,567 --> 00:06:49,100
It's alarming.

125
00:06:49,233 --> 00:06:52,100
The drug situation
keeps escalating.

126
00:06:52,233 --> 00:06:57,367
And the masterminds
they seem to be slipping away.

127
00:06:57,500 --> 00:07:00,367
So, be careful,

128
00:07:00,500 --> 00:07:04,667
because people like that don't
forget names and faces.

129
00:07:06,500 --> 00:07:07,300
Brother's here.

130
00:07:07,433 --> 00:07:08,733
[UNEASY MUSIC PLAYING]

131
00:07:08,867 --> 00:07:10,633
Hon, let's eat.

132
00:07:10,767 --> 00:07:17,267
[UNEASY MUSIC CONTINUES]

133
00:07:18,300 --> 00:07:19,900
[GUN FIRING]

134
00:07:20,033 --> 00:07:22,000
<i> Castro, let's go!</i>

135
00:07:23,167 --> 00:07:25,767
[UNEASY MUSIC CONTINUES]

136
00:07:25,900 --> 00:07:30,000
Andrew was telling me
about his coverage in the north.

137
00:07:30,133 --> 00:07:31,433
Drug deal.

138
00:07:31,567 --> 00:07:37,333
Unfortunately,
the mastermind escaped again.

139
00:07:37,467 --> 00:07:38,500
Yeah.

140
00:07:39,733 --> 00:07:41,067
How about you, Tomas?
How are you?

141
00:07:42,500 --> 00:07:44,200
Busy? Where did you come from?

142
00:07:45,333 --> 00:07:46,733
From a meeting.

143
00:07:48,533 --> 00:07:49,300
How was it?

144
00:07:49,433 --> 00:07:50,967
Was the deal finalized?

145
00:07:52,367 --> 00:07:54,933
Unfortunately, not.

146
00:07:55,067 --> 00:07:56,433
There was interference.

147
00:07:56,567 --> 00:07:57,967
A client withdrew.

148
00:07:58,100 --> 00:08:00,500
Oh, that's unfortunate.

149
00:08:00,633 --> 00:08:03,200
Well, that's business.

150
00:08:03,333 --> 00:08:05,500
There will be others, Hon.

151
00:08:05,633 --> 00:08:09,867
Yeah, but the one who interfered
must pay.

152
00:08:13,367 --> 00:08:14,667
Tomas, is that blood?

153
00:08:14,800 --> 00:08:21,400
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

154
00:08:23,533 --> 00:08:26,167
Dad, does the chief know
about your plan

155
00:08:26,300 --> 00:08:27,533
to show yourself to mom?

156
00:08:28,300 --> 00:08:29,533
Yes.

157
00:08:30,367 --> 00:08:31,967
I asked permission. He knows.

158
00:08:32,933 --> 00:08:35,267
Does this mean you'll reveal
yourself?

159
00:08:35,400 --> 00:08:36,600
We'll be together again?

160
00:08:36,733 --> 00:08:37,833
No, dear.

161
00:08:37,967 --> 00:08:38,867
[DRAMATIC MUSIC PLAYING]

162
00:08:39,000 --> 00:08:41,033
I need to finish the mission.

163
00:08:44,100 --> 00:08:47,000
I only came here to see you.

164
00:08:49,033 --> 00:08:51,733
I don't want to see you hurt,
Clarissa.

165
00:08:54,000 --> 00:08:56,267
I promise, after this mission,

166
00:08:57,933 --> 00:08:59,867
Berdugo will be imprisoned

167
00:09:00,000 --> 00:09:02,567
and our family will finally
be complete.

168
00:09:05,533 --> 00:09:07,800
Clarissa, we're almost there.

169
00:09:09,767 --> 00:09:11,600
Joey, we're close.

170
00:09:12,733 --> 00:09:14,033
I hope so.

171
00:09:14,167 --> 00:09:16,100
I hope this is it.

172
00:09:16,233 --> 00:09:25,567
[DRAMATIC MUSIC CONTINUES]

173
00:09:31,800 --> 00:09:33,700
Why, Hon?
Where were you wounded?

174
00:09:33,833 --> 00:09:35,733
There was...

175
00:09:35,867 --> 00:09:38,367
a branch on the driveway.

176
00:09:39,667 --> 00:09:41,000
I wasn't looking.

177
00:09:41,133 --> 00:09:43,500
Hon, you have to be careful.

178
00:09:43,633 --> 00:09:44,900
That has to be cleaned.

179
00:09:45,033 --> 00:09:46,467
- Let me help you.
- It's okay, it's okay.

180
00:09:46,600 --> 00:09:47,433
I got this.

181
00:09:48,500 --> 00:09:50,100
I'll just change the bandage.

182
00:09:52,333 --> 00:09:54,633
Don't leave Andrew.

183
00:09:54,767 --> 00:09:56,900
He rarely eats with company.

184
00:09:59,000 --> 00:10:00,367
Okay.

185
00:10:00,500 --> 00:10:09,633
[STIRRING MUSIC CONTINUES]

186
00:10:12,867 --> 00:10:14,533
Tomas is really...

187
00:10:14,667 --> 00:10:17,367
He hates being fussed over.

188
00:10:20,133 --> 00:10:21,933
[INQUISITIVE MUSIC PLAYING]

189
00:10:22,067 --> 00:10:23,233
Why?

190
00:10:23,367 --> 00:10:25,567
What's wrong, Andrew?

191
00:10:25,700 --> 00:10:28,867
Sister, it's not just a small
wound.

192
00:10:29,000 --> 00:10:31,433
Brother's wound is deep.

193
00:10:31,567 --> 00:10:34,833
You better talk to him
or at least observe him.

194
00:10:35,000 --> 00:10:36,767
What do you mean?

195
00:10:36,900 --> 00:10:41,800
Maybe he has a problem
he doesn't want to tell us.

196
00:10:43,300 --> 00:10:44,300
Okay.

197
00:10:45,767 --> 00:10:47,600
I'll talk to him.

198
00:10:47,733 --> 00:10:52,633
And I really appreciate
your concern for Tomas.

199
00:10:55,400 --> 00:10:56,900
You were right.

200
00:10:57,033 --> 00:10:59,300
It was Berdugo who made
the deal in the north.

201
00:10:59,667 --> 00:11:02,400
I even heard Delilah
mention his alias.

202
00:11:02,533 --> 00:11:05,200
<i>We need to talk
because next time,</i>

203
00:11:05,333 --> 00:11:06,800
<i>you'll be the one I'll speak to.</i>

204
00:11:06,933 --> 00:11:09,100
<i>But of course, if you permit,
Berdugo.</i>

205
00:11:09,267 --> 00:11:10,100
<i> Certainly.</i>

206
00:11:10,233 --> 00:11:11,500
It's just frustrating.

207
00:11:11,633 --> 00:11:13,300
I was there for so long,
I didn't see his face.

208
00:11:13,433 --> 00:11:15,333
Child, don't worry.

209
00:11:15,467 --> 00:11:16,433
That's okay.

210
00:11:16,567 --> 00:11:18,133
What matters is you're alive.

211
00:11:18,267 --> 00:11:20,433
I was so worried about you.

212
00:11:20,567 --> 00:11:23,567
I wanted to help,
but I couldn't do anything.

213
00:11:23,700 --> 00:11:25,933
That's why I just texted you
earlier.

214
00:11:27,067 --> 00:11:28,467
Yes, Dad.

215
00:11:29,800 --> 00:11:32,533
But why did it seem like only
DDE agents were there?

216
00:11:32,667 --> 00:11:33,767
There were no police.

217
00:11:33,900 --> 00:11:36,600
<i>Sir, positive.
Berdugo is at the resort.</i>

218
00:11:38,067 --> 00:11:40,233
<i>Why aren't the other police
moving?</i>

219
00:11:40,533 --> 00:11:42,200
<i>Because we also have
confirmation</i>

220
00:11:42,367 --> 00:11:45,367
<i>that one of our men is involved
in the syndicate, it's Castro.</i>

221
00:11:45,500 --> 00:11:48,200
<i>It is a bad enough image
for the police.</i>

222
00:11:48,333 --> 00:11:50,500
<i>We need to compartmentalize
the operation</i>

223
00:11:50,633 --> 00:11:52,767
<i> so no information leaks.</i>

224
00:11:52,900 --> 00:11:56,900
<i>That's why no police,
only DDE agents.</i>

225
00:11:57,033 --> 00:11:57,900
<i> But, Sir...</i>

226
00:11:58,033 --> 00:11:59,800
<i>Miguel, don't attempt
to charge in.</i>

227
00:11:59,933 --> 00:12:02,233
<i>You'll waste everything
you've worked for.</i>

228
00:12:02,367 --> 00:12:04,400
<i>Do not blow your cover,
Major Delgado.</i>

229
00:12:04,533 --> 00:12:05,967
<i> That's an order!</i>

230
00:12:06,100 --> 00:12:09,100
I wanted to tell you and Andrew,
but I couldn't.

231
00:12:09,233 --> 00:12:10,533
There's protocol.

232
00:12:10,667 --> 00:12:12,233
Does Andrew know about this?

233
00:12:12,367 --> 00:12:14,067
He has to, he's in media.

234
00:12:15,233 --> 00:12:17,267
He hasn't mentioned anything
to me.

235
00:12:17,400 --> 00:12:22,033
His agent friend, Zoey,
knows a lot.

236
00:12:24,267 --> 00:12:25,967
Gosh, Andrew.

237
00:12:26,100 --> 00:12:28,533
You didn't even tell me
you were back,

238
00:12:28,667 --> 00:12:31,467
then suddenly you call
for a meeting?

239
00:12:31,600 --> 00:12:33,067
What if I had a date?

240
00:12:34,500 --> 00:12:35,800
Wait, you actually have a date?

241
00:12:36,333 --> 00:12:38,467
Just "what if," Boss.

242
00:12:42,700 --> 00:12:46,067
Anyway, the reason I called
for a meeting

243
00:12:46,200 --> 00:12:47,300
is because I want
to walk you through

244
00:12:47,433 --> 00:12:48,700
what happened in the north.

245
00:12:48,967 --> 00:12:51,267
I want us aligned
because starting tomorrow,

246
00:12:51,400 --> 00:12:53,233
that's where our coverage
will revolve.

247
00:12:53,367 --> 00:12:54,333
Confirmed.

248
00:12:54,467 --> 00:12:56,533
Berdugo was there.

249
00:13:00,933 --> 00:13:02,233
That's him.

250
00:13:02,367 --> 00:13:06,500
[INQUISITIVE MUSIC PLAYING]

251
00:13:08,233 --> 00:13:09,867
He's handsome, isn't he?

252
00:13:10,800 --> 00:13:11,867
What?

253
00:13:14,467 --> 00:13:16,233
But that's just his back.

254
00:13:16,367 --> 00:13:18,633
The shot is far,
and he's wearing a hat.

255
00:13:18,767 --> 00:13:20,767
How do we build a case
with that?

256
00:13:20,900 --> 00:13:22,267
No face, no profile.

257
00:13:24,733 --> 00:13:28,667
Your ex-lover slash TOTGA
in DDE, Boss,

258
00:13:28,800 --> 00:13:30,433
she has no visual ID?

259
00:13:31,900 --> 00:13:33,400
None.

260
00:13:34,967 --> 00:13:35,800
But...

261
00:13:39,267 --> 00:13:45,167
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

262
00:13:45,300 --> 00:13:46,500
I found this.

263
00:13:47,800 --> 00:13:50,500
I found this when Berdugo
was escaping.

264
00:13:52,267 --> 00:13:53,867
Looks expensive.

265
00:13:54,000 --> 00:13:55,500
Exactly.

266
00:13:55,667 --> 00:13:58,567
Men like him
don't wear generic things.

267
00:13:58,700 --> 00:14:01,500
And high-end accessories
are easier to trace

268
00:14:01,633 --> 00:14:03,867
because there are fewer
suppliers.

269
00:14:04,000 --> 00:14:05,000
Yes.

270
00:14:05,133 --> 00:14:08,100
So, we don't chase the man.
We chase his tastes.

271
00:14:08,233 --> 00:14:09,200
Yes.

272
00:14:10,500 --> 00:14:12,333
Can I see it, Boss.

273
00:14:12,467 --> 00:14:19,067
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC CONTINUES]

274
00:14:21,433 --> 00:14:23,367
There's an engraving...

275
00:14:23,500 --> 00:14:24,567
A brand?

276
00:14:26,300 --> 00:14:28,333
Well, that's what I thought too.

277
00:14:28,500 --> 00:14:32,633
But I tried reverse searching.
Nothing, no brand identified.

278
00:14:32,767 --> 00:14:35,233
Are we sure this is a brand?

279
00:14:35,367 --> 00:14:38,933
Men like Berdugo,
they're narcissistic.

280
00:14:39,067 --> 00:14:40,200
This could be initials.

281
00:14:40,333 --> 00:14:42,000
Even their towels have initials.

282
00:14:42,133 --> 00:14:43,867
Possible, possible, yes.

283
00:14:45,300 --> 00:14:48,200
And Joey, wasn't she with you
on this mission?

284
00:14:49,400 --> 00:14:51,067
Does she know about this
cufflink?

285
00:14:51,200 --> 00:14:52,233
Not yet.

286
00:14:53,333 --> 00:14:55,000
I owe her.

287
00:14:57,133 --> 00:15:00,567
So, while this isn't solid,
she doesn't have to know.

288
00:15:00,700 --> 00:15:04,133
She needs answers.
She doesn't need another risk.

289
00:15:04,833 --> 00:15:08,933
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC CONTINUES]

290
00:15:11,867 --> 00:15:14,233
Nothing was explained to me.

291
00:15:14,867 --> 00:15:17,267
I can't just stand idle.

292
00:15:17,400 --> 00:15:23,167
So, when I learned Berdugo
was selling drugs to Delilah,

293
00:15:23,300 --> 00:15:25,900
I searched it in this notebook.

294
00:15:27,633 --> 00:15:29,167
Here, I found it.

295
00:15:30,600 --> 00:15:32,367
Lumen-X?

296
00:15:32,500 --> 00:15:34,500
I heard that from them.

297
00:15:34,667 --> 00:15:39,000
Yes, that's a party drug.
Popular among the youth.

298
00:15:40,033 --> 00:15:41,200
What is this?

299
00:15:41,333 --> 00:15:44,233
Why is there a drawing of a
mushroom with "2019" written?

300
00:15:45,467 --> 00:15:47,600
Maybe Ramon made this

301
00:15:47,733 --> 00:15:52,267
because Lumen-X has a component
from magic mushrooms.

302
00:15:53,800 --> 00:15:55,167
The effect is potent.

303
00:15:55,300 --> 00:15:57,333
You'll hallucinate.

304
00:15:57,467 --> 00:16:00,533
That's why I did surveillance
on underground sellers

305
00:16:00,667 --> 00:16:02,767
of magic mushrooms.

306
00:16:02,900 --> 00:16:07,267
Maybe it would lead me
to Berdugo's laboratory.

307
00:16:07,400 --> 00:16:09,000
Did you find it?

308
00:16:10,433 --> 00:16:11,400
No.

309
00:16:12,633 --> 00:16:15,900
But I won't stop
until they're imprisoned.

310
00:16:19,367 --> 00:16:20,933
My fellow<i> Tirada</i> viewers,

311
00:16:21,067 --> 00:16:27,067
Lumen-X is the drug destroying
the lives of the youth today.

312
00:16:27,200 --> 00:16:28,933
This man with his back turned...

313
00:16:29,067 --> 00:16:32,900
[INQUISITIVE MUSIC PLAYING]

314
00:16:33,900 --> 00:16:35,867
That's Berdugo,

315
00:16:36,000 --> 00:16:39,233
the creator of this damn drug.

316
00:16:40,900 --> 00:16:43,300
He escaped the operation
in the north,

317
00:16:43,467 --> 00:16:46,600
but I'm certain his world
is shrinking.

318
00:16:47,967 --> 00:16:51,867
And next time,
there will be no escape.

319
00:16:52,967 --> 00:16:54,867
It's prison time.

320
00:16:57,467 --> 00:16:59,833
You can count on it,
fellow<i> Tirada</i> viewers.

321
00:17:01,867 --> 00:17:03,233
As always.

322
00:17:04,300 --> 00:17:06,367
[INQUISITIVE MUSIC CONTINUES]

323
00:17:06,500 --> 00:17:08,167
- Okay.
- Nice. Solid.

324
00:17:08,300 --> 00:17:09,333
Beautiful, beautiful,
beautiful.

325
00:17:09,467 --> 00:17:12,167
[CHUCKLES]

326
00:17:12,300 --> 00:17:13,800
I thought I was brave,

327
00:17:13,933 --> 00:17:17,100
but that's the real courage
of Boss Idol.

328
00:17:17,267 --> 00:17:19,067
[CHUCKLES]

329
00:17:21,767 --> 00:17:22,733
Just passionate.

330
00:17:23,900 --> 00:17:27,300
Ma'am Zoey, he's not only
passionate in tirades...

331
00:17:27,433 --> 00:17:29,000
if you know what I mean.

332
00:17:29,133 --> 00:17:30,567
Hey, gross!

333
00:17:30,700 --> 00:17:32,133
Why?

334
00:17:32,267 --> 00:17:34,300
In love! Passionate in...

335
00:17:34,433 --> 00:17:36,067
Right? Love, right?

336
00:17:36,200 --> 00:17:37,767
- Love?
- Right, Boss?

337
00:17:37,900 --> 00:17:39,700
Yes, good thing you clarified.

338
00:17:42,500 --> 00:17:44,200
And besides, we're not even sure

339
00:17:44,333 --> 00:17:46,333
if it's the right "oey"
we're teasing.

340
00:17:46,467 --> 00:17:49,333
Yes, true. Sounds like it.

341
00:17:49,500 --> 00:17:51,300
This one, Zoey.

342
00:17:51,433 --> 00:17:53,200
The other one...

343
00:17:53,333 --> 00:17:54,633
Oey?

344
00:17:54,767 --> 00:17:57,100
So clever.

345
00:17:57,233 --> 00:17:59,467
Oey?
[CHUCKLES AWKWARDLY]

346
00:18:00,667 --> 00:18:02,633
Okay, okay. Are you happy now?

347
00:18:02,767 --> 00:18:04,767
Just joking, Boss.

348
00:18:04,900 --> 00:18:06,367
You're teasing me again.

349
00:18:06,500 --> 00:18:07,467
It's just a joke.

350
00:18:07,600 --> 00:18:11,067
Anyway, you two, if it's okay,
step out for now,

351
00:18:11,200 --> 00:18:13,133
especially you.

352
00:18:13,267 --> 00:18:15,133
Be careful,
you might lose your job.

353
00:18:15,267 --> 00:18:18,367
All right, I'm going, I'm going.

354
00:18:18,500 --> 00:18:19,700
We'll leave you for now.

355
00:18:19,833 --> 00:18:21,033
Boss...

356
00:18:24,533 --> 00:18:30,533
[ENGINE WHIRRING]

357
00:18:32,400 --> 00:18:35,367
Do you think Andrew suspected
anything?

358
00:18:36,900 --> 00:18:39,067
He didn't ask anything directly.

359
00:18:41,400 --> 00:18:45,400
But I saw he was contemplating.

360
00:18:45,533 --> 00:18:47,800
But since we're brothers-in-law,

361
00:18:49,133 --> 00:18:52,400
he won't think I'm Berdugo.

362
00:18:52,533 --> 00:18:58,033
That idea is too far
of what I am to him.

363
00:18:58,200 --> 00:19:00,967
But, Boss, he's getting closer
and closer.

364
00:19:01,100 --> 00:19:02,200
I know.

365
00:19:03,267 --> 00:19:04,700
And he's smart.

366
00:19:05,867 --> 00:19:09,100
Once he smells something,
he won't let go.

367
00:19:09,233 --> 00:19:11,900
Like I said, he's obsessed.

368
00:19:12,033 --> 00:19:15,400
If he won't stop,
then we must push harder.

369
00:19:15,533 --> 00:19:19,567
Boss, the operation cannot stop.

370
00:19:19,700 --> 00:19:22,567
Boss, I don't mean to get ahead
of you,

371
00:19:22,700 --> 00:19:25,367
but there's only one question
you need to answer.

372
00:19:25,500 --> 00:19:27,833
Which is more important?

373
00:19:28,000 --> 00:19:29,833
Andrew...

374
00:19:29,967 --> 00:19:31,367
or your business?

375
00:19:33,567 --> 00:19:34,700
Sorry about that, okay?

376
00:19:35,233 --> 00:19:36,533
It's fine.

377
00:19:37,967 --> 00:19:40,867
I didn't know they were aware
of whatever you

378
00:19:41,000 --> 00:19:42,767
and Joey have.

379
00:19:42,900 --> 00:19:43,867
That's nothing.

380
00:19:44,000 --> 00:19:45,733
They link me to everyone anyway.

381
00:19:45,867 --> 00:19:47,333
We're all single.

382
00:19:47,467 --> 00:19:48,533
[ZOEY CHUCKLES SOFTLY]

383
00:19:50,900 --> 00:19:52,500
What brought you here?

384
00:19:55,067 --> 00:19:57,833
Since the operation
in the north is over,

385
00:19:59,100 --> 00:20:02,200
I just want to apologize
for how things went.

386
00:20:03,667 --> 00:20:08,667
If I made you or Joey
uncomfortable.

387
00:20:08,800 --> 00:20:11,933
Since we're talking
about this again,

388
00:20:12,067 --> 00:20:14,700
I need to clarify something.

389
00:20:14,833 --> 00:20:18,733
[DREAMY MUSIC PLAYING]

390
00:20:20,267 --> 00:20:21,800
About?

391
00:20:25,800 --> 00:20:27,400
Anyway,

392
00:20:27,533 --> 00:20:30,533
just check the new batch
of Lumen-X.

393
00:20:32,100 --> 00:20:33,367
You're not coming?

394
00:20:33,500 --> 00:20:35,900
I don't want to be late
for my meeting.

395
00:20:36,067 --> 00:20:38,933
I trust you and Lisa.

396
00:20:39,067 --> 00:20:41,800
I thought you wanted
to see it too?

397
00:20:41,933 --> 00:20:43,900
And to answer your question,

398
00:20:46,100 --> 00:20:51,200
nothing is more important to me
than my family,

399
00:20:52,267 --> 00:20:54,600
and the business
that sustains us.

400
00:20:55,800 --> 00:20:57,533
Find a way to get rid of him.

401
00:20:59,000 --> 00:21:01,433
No trace, no noise.

402
00:21:01,567 --> 00:21:03,233
My pleasure, Boss.

403
00:21:04,767 --> 00:21:14,133
[INQUISITIVE MUSIC PLAYING]

404
00:21:14,300 --> 00:21:19,667
[UPBEAT MUSIC PLAYING]

405
00:21:19,800 --> 00:21:22,933
Do you remember the brown
stuffed bear?

406
00:21:23,067 --> 00:21:24,633
Why do you need that?

407
00:21:24,767 --> 00:21:25,800
It's not for you.

408
00:21:25,933 --> 00:21:26,900
You know, girl, try this.

409
00:21:27,033 --> 00:21:28,200
Crispy mushroom.

410
00:21:28,333 --> 00:21:29,533
Did you get what I sent?

411
00:21:29,667 --> 00:21:32,000
The logo and the number
in Ramon's notebook.

412
00:21:32,133 --> 00:21:34,200
Won't this be a hindrance
to our operation?

413
00:21:34,333 --> 00:21:36,800
If sabotage was my intention...

414
00:21:36,933 --> 00:21:38,567
I'm not talking to you!

415
00:21:38,700 --> 00:21:40,500
So many operations
have already failed.

416
00:21:40,633 --> 00:21:42,433
What are you doing there
in Sta. Isabel?

417
00:21:42,600 --> 00:21:45,700
Sir, I feel Berdugo's laboratory
is here.

418
00:21:45,833 --> 00:21:47,567
Ma'am Yvette said she'll have me
brought there.

419
00:21:47,700 --> 00:21:48,400
But I'm thinking...

420
00:21:48,533 --> 00:21:49,233
What about you?

421
00:21:49,367 --> 00:21:50,867
I'll bring Joey there.

422
00:21:51,000 --> 00:21:53,767
Tell her who you really are.
